  "configuration_id": "config_016",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only models (0.485–0.520) substantially outperform image-only (0.208), and scvi_n200 > pca_n2000 for RNA encoding. The critical unresolved question is whether multimodal fusion adds value at all, given how weak the image modality is in isolation. Config_016 (multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, concat) is a clean ablation against config_001 (same RNA encoder, same profile setting) with the only change being the addition of resnet50 image features via concat fusion. This directly tests whether the image modality contributes complementary signal or introduces noise. Resolving this early is the highest-value use of the next experiment: if multimodal does not improve over RNA-only, an entire branch (~36 configs) can be deprioritized, freeing budget for RNA-only multiprofile and scgpt experiments. If it does help, we gain a validated direction to exploit with better encoders and fusion strategies."
}

